# Fixed 2026-10-02, defect 130's class, lane recovery-b8 (lane recovery-b6's
# shape beside its 130 (e), `lc12_block_multi`). Symptom: a C block comment
# over two lines, `/* one` over `two */`, cost four messages for one comment,
# the second line's margin, a join, a missing expression and an orphan
# block, where the same comment on one line costs one. Cause: the lexer read
# a `/*` as a comment only where its `*/` stood on the same line, and
# anything else as code. Now a `/*` whose `*/` ends a later line is one
# comment from one to the other, told once, its certain fix writing a `#`
# line for each of its lines with words, at the margin of the `/*`'s line,
# a javadoc `*` dropped.

#~v unexpected_character
# The entry point,
# which prints.
function main()
    #~v unexpected_character
    # one
    # two
    print(1)
    x = 1
    print(x)
    #~v unexpected_character
    # y = f(1,
    #~v unexpected_character
    # a
    # b  # and a note after it
    #~v unexpected_character
    # c
    # d
    print(2)
